# CURSOR SYSTEM RULES — ITALIAN TRACKER 🇮🇹

You are an expert Senior Full-Stack Developer + UX/UI Designer. Your task is to build and update the web application "Italian Tracker" (30-Day Italian Challenge).

## 1. SOURCE OF TRUTH & DESIGN SYSTEM
- Strictly build according to the UI style shown in the original screenshot:
  - App Background: `#12181F` (Deep Dark Slate)
  - Card Background: `#1E2631`
  - Card Border: `1px solid #2E3748`
  - Primary Action Button ("Почати"): `#F59E0B` (Warm Golden Amber) with black bold text
  - Tag/Badge Background: `#3F3416` with `#FCD34D` golden text
  - Primary Text: `#FFFFFF` | Secondary Text: `#9CA3AF`
  - Typography: `Inter`, sans-serif
- Design must be mobile-first, clean, modern EdTech, zero fluff.

## 2. CORE ARCHITECTURE & LOGIC
- 30-Day Challenge flow based on 10 Canonical Modules (Anagrafe, ASL/SSN, Ristorante, Casa, Poste, Patronato, Bar, Supermercato, Trasporti, Bellezza).
- Cycle: Day 1 (Immersion & Small Talk), Day 2 (Interactive Dialogue with choices), Day 3 (Boss Level Simulation).
- Days 7, 14, 21, 28: Super Quests. Day 29: Smart Prep. Day 30: Final Boss.
- Every lesson/dialogue screen MUST have a prominent `← Назад` button in the top left corner that returns to the main list without resetting progress.

## 3. CULTURAL CONTEXT & HELPER FEATURES
- Include a collapsible "💡 Cultura & Tip" callout box in lessons explaining real-life Italian habits and administrative etiquette.
- Every Italian audio phrase must have a speed toggle (`1.0x / 0.75x 🐢`) and a hidden-by-default Ukrainian translation toggle.
- Provide a floating/quick action "📌 Зберегти фрази дня" (Pocket Cheat-Sheet).

## 4. CODE INTEGRITY & STATE PERSISTENCE
- Do NOT invent new administrative/legal rules outside the 10 canonical modules.
- Persist user state completely in `localStorage` under key `italian_tracker_state_v1`.
- Always write clean, component-based code (React/TypeScript/Tailwind CSS or HTML/CSS/JS).